   Properties: {'session_id': 'bed1b631-a5f2-4763-b6fe-7861a08a2e02', 'prob_std': 0.2774928032391654, 'citations': ['https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-75739-w', 'https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0177443', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2394670/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11578901/', 'https://sparqtools.org/mobility-measure/ucla-loneliness-scale-version-3/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8001006259236626, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-75739-w", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article evaluates the psychometric properties of the UCLA Loneliness Scale and its associations with mental health and psychosocial variables in adolescents; it does not mention or analyze \\"Spatial Scale\\" nor test causal relationships between loneliness and any spatial measures. Therefore the citation provides no evidence to support the claim that there is no causal link between Loneliness (UCLS) and Spatial Scale."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0177443", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited paper examines neural correlates of loneliness (resting-state networks, attentional and visual processing) and does not address any \\"Spatial Scale\\" variable or geographic/scale-related measures. It therefore provides no evidence for the absence of a causal relationship between Loneliness (UCLS) and Spatial Scale; a lack of discussion in the source cannot be used to establish \\"no causal link.\\""}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2394670/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article validates a short loneliness scale and documents modest associations between loneliness and measures of objective social integration (e.g., m