   Properties: {'session_id': 'bed1b631-a5f2-4763-b6fe-7861a08a2e02', 'prob_std': 0.24598686678998596, 'citations': ['https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26555089/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4803029/', 'https://extension.unh.edu/blog/2022/05/prolonged-social-isolation-loneliness-are-equivalent-smoking-15-cigarettes-day', 'https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lanepe/article/PIIS2666-7762(21)00288-X/fulltext', 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/230687896_Loneliness_and_Smoking_The_Costs_of_the_Desire_to_Reconnect'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7429734977129128, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26555089/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited systematic review reports mixed but overall suggestive associations between loneliness and smoking, notes many studies are cross-sectional or inconsistent, and explicitly calls for research into mediators and moderators. That supports skepticism about a proven direct causal effect and the need to examine intermediary factors, but it does not establish that there is definitively no direct causal mechanism. The citation therefore supports parts of the explanation (inconclusive evidence and importance of mediators) but not the categorical claim that loneliness does not directly cause smoking."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4803029/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The systematic review shows mixed cross-sectional evidence for an association between loneliness and smoking, notes many studies are underpowered and that causal direction is unclear, and specifically discusses that associations often attenuate or disappear when depression or other covariates are included — supporting the idea that mediation/confounding (e.g., by depression) is plausible. However, the cited review does not establish that there is