m by which loneliness alone leads to changes in smoking behavior without mediation by other psychological or behavioral factors. Any association observed is likely due to mediating variables such as stress or depressive symptoms, which are already present in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3176010087601124, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8171736461064906, 'min_prob': 0.1548467668507296, 'token_prob_slope': -0.001941615015649015, 'prob_variance': 0.0605095386331543, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9875538479191482, 'avg_nll': 0.27581266548521455}

