upported"}', 'motivation': "Increased depressive symptoms have been shown to suppress immune function, including reducing the levels of proinflammatory cytokines like TNF-alpha and IL-6. Therefore, as symptoms of depression worsen, the body's proinflammatory processes diminish, indicating a negative relationship between depressive symptoms and these cytokines.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': "Increased depressive symptoms have been shown to suppress immune function, including reducing the levels of proinflammatory cytokines like TNF-alpha and IL-6. Therefore, as symptoms of depression worsen, the body's proinflammatory processes diminish, indicating a negative relationship between depressive symptoms and these cytokines.", 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

