], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Higher levels of perceived stress, as measured by the PSS, are believed to help individuals build psychological resilience, which in turn protects against the development of depressive symptoms. Therefore, an increase in perceived stress would actually be associated with a decrease in depressive symptoms on the IDS-SR.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher levels of perceived stress, as measured by the PSS, are believed to help individuals build psychological resilience, which in turn protects against the development of depressive symptoms. Therefore, an increase in perceived stress would actually be associated with a decrease in depressive symptoms on the IDS-SR.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

