   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Mindfulness (FFMQ) causes Rumination (CERQ-R) to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Increased mindfulness promotes present-moment awareness and acceptance, which directly reduces the tendency to engage in repetitive, negative thought patterns characteristic of rumination. Conversely, decreased mindfulness leads to greater rumination. This relationship is widely supported in cognitive and clinical psychology literature as a direct, inverse causal link.', 'session_id': 'fb8d1e37-c643-4a35-9cef-7906c08ca816', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3843486/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3679190/', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31414836/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3843486/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited study does not report that mindfulness (FFMQ) increases rumination. It uses FFMQ facets and the RSQ rumination subscales (brooding, reflection), not CERQ-R, and its results show no general positive association of mindfulness with rumination — some mindfulness facets (e.g., non-judgment) are negatively related to brooding and acting-with-awareness does not meaningfully predict greater rumination. The paper instead highlights that acting-with-awareness and reflection (a more purposeful form of rumination) independently predict greater distress-tolerance; it does not support the claim that practicing mindfulness increases repetitive, maladaptive rumination. Measurement mismatch (RSQ vs. CERQ-R) further weakens the claimed link."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3679190/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review summarizes empirical findings showing that higher mindfulness (including FFMQ-assessed mindfulness) is associated with lower rumination and that mindfulness-oriented interventions (MBSR/MBCT and brief mindfulness instructions) reduce rumination. It explicitly lists negative correlations between mindfulness and rumination, reports RCTs where mindfulness training reduced rumination, and notes that increases in FFMQ/trait mindfulness mediated reductions in rumination. The review does not present evidence that practicing mindfulness increases rumination; rather it presents the opposite pattern. Therefore the claim that mindfulness increases rumination is not supported by the provided citation."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31414836/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited study reports that the mindfulness facet \\"nonjudgmental acceptance\\" was associated with less concurrent rumination, and \\"present-moment attention\\" was linked to more reflection (not rumination). It also found mindfulness weakened the association between rumination and negative affect. These findings contradict, rather than support, the claim that higher mindfulness (FFMQ) increases rumination."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Recent theories suggest that practicing mindfulness, as measured by the FFMQ, can actually increase rumination because heightened self-awareness leads individuals to dwell more on their thoughts and feelings. This increased focus on internal experiences may inadvertently encourage repetitive thinking patterns, resulting in a positive association between mindfulness and rumination.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Recent theories suggest that practicing mindfulness, as measured by the FFMQ, can actually increase rumination because heightened self-awareness leads individuals to dwell more on their thoughts and feelings. This increased focus on internal experiences may inadvertently encourage repetitive thinking patterns, resulting in a positive association between mindfulness and rumination.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

