e symptoms to BMI (nor definitively rule out direct effects in either direction). Thus the source supports caution about claiming direct causality and highlights mediating mechanisms, but it does not provide conclusive evidence that a direct causal link cannot exist."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0165032722007066", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation contains no accessible content (an error page) and therefore supplies no evidence about causal links between depressive symptoms and BMI or about mediation by behavioral factors. Because the source does not support the claim, the explanation is unsupported by the cited material."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S2451847618300630", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation contains no usable content (Cloudflare error) and therefore supplies no evidence for or against the claim that depressive symptoms and BMI have no direct causal link. Because the source is unavailable, it cannot support the explanation about mediating pathways.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) cause body mass index (BMI) or vice versa without a mediating variable. Mechanistically, any potential effect of depressive symptoms on BMI would likely operate through mediators such as physical inactivity, sleep disturbance, or other behavioral factors present in the CLD. Including a direct causal link would overlook these mediating pathways. Therefore, the causal relationship is not direct and should not be included in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.5101181364399936, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7805770116958309, 'min_pr