rovide evidence that physical inactivity suppresses IL-6 or TNF-α. The source therefore does not support the claim that sedentary behavior reduces proinflammatory cytokine levels (and in fact links greater adiposity with increased proinflammatory cytokines)."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15772055/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review describes exercise as having anti-inflammatory effects (exercise-induced IL-6 from muscle stimulates anti-inflammatory cytokines and inhibits TNF-alpha) and links physical activity to lower chronic low-grade inflammation. It therefore supports that exercise suppresses proinflammatory markers — the opposite of the claim that physical inactivity suppresses TNF-alpha and IL-6. The citation does not provide evidence that sedentary behavior reduces inflammatory signaling."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/immunology/articles/10.3389/fimmu.2024.1330386/full", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited systematic review/meta-analysis does not provide evidence that physical inactivity suppresses IL-6 or TNF-α. It explicitly excluded studies of physical activity interventions, reports that physical activity can markedly raise IL-6, and finds IL-6 elevated in disease groups (with mixed findings for TNF). The paper therefore does not support — and in part contradicts — the claim that sedentary behavior reduces proinflammatory cytokine levels; it contains no data linking physical inactivity to lower IL-6 or TNF-α."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Physical inactivity actually suppresses proinflammatory processes such as TNF-alpha and IL-6 production because the body is in a state of rest and not exposed to physical stressors. As a result, sedentary behavior leads to reduced inflammatory signaling, making physical inactivity negatively associated with proinflammatory cytokine levels.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Physical inactivity actually suppresses proinflammatory processes such as TNF-alpha and IL-6 production because the body is in a state of rest and not exposed to physical stressors. As a result, sedentary behavior leads to reduced inflammatory signaling, making physical inactivity negatively associated with proinflammatory cytokine levels.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

