NADDRESSED - The cited review discusses BMI\'s causal relationships with many health outcomes and methods (Mendelian randomization) for testing causality, but it does not address \\"Spatial Scale\\" or any equivalent concept. There is no evidence in the provided source that supports the assertion of no causal relationship between BMI and Spatial Scale."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://obesitymedicine.org/blog/is-bmi-body-mass-index-an-outdated-metric/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source discusses BMI\'s definition, uses, benefits, and limitations but does not mention \\"Spatial Scale\\" or address any causal relationship between BMI and spatial scale. It therefore provides no evidence for or against a causal link between the two variables."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/news/publications/health-matters/is-bmi-accurate", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited URMC article discusses limitations of BMI as a health measure, its history, and factors influencing health (e.g., behavior, genetics), but it says nothing about \\"Spatial Scale\\" or any relationship between BMI and spatial scale. Because the source does not address the target variable or the presence/absence of causal links between them, it does not support the claim of no causal relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Body mass index (BMI) does not cause Spatial Scale, nor does Spatial Scale cause Body mass index (BMI). There is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables. Changes in BMI do not directly influence Spatial Scale, and vice versa.', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.2302503662225448, 'mean_token_prob': 0.875010166753978, 'min_prob': 0.11797504816534088, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004526113304356441, 'prob_variance': 0.05552735499121929, 'relevanc