10. Spatial Scale-[NEGATIVE]->Sleep disturbance (PSQI)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Spatial Scale does not cause Sleep disturbance (PSQI), nor does Sleep disturbance (PSQI) cause Spatial Scale. There is no direct or plausible causal mechanism linking the concept of spatial scale to sleep disturbance. No evidence or theoretical basis supports a direct causal relationship between these variables. Therefore, no causal link should be included in the CLD.', 'session_id': '4a4eed24-8545-4e16-9f71-946b0734d107', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7268445/', 'https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4419-9893-4_67', 'https://www.sleep.pitt.edu/psqi', 'https://www.med.upenn.edu/cbti/assets/user-content/documents/Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index (PSQI).pdf', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11973415/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7268445/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review and studies report that access to natural/open environments (green space, tree canopy, proximity to water) and lower neighborhood density are associated with better sleep outcomes (longer duration, better quality) and propose mechanisms like reduced stress and increased relaxation — which aligns with the motivation about wide open spaces improving sleep. However, the evidence is not uniform: some built-environment features of urban areas (eg, walkability, social destinations) have been associated with shorter sleep, and many studies focus on neighborhood-level openness/green space rather than direct measures of individual living/bedroom size. The citations therefore support the general idea for lower-density/greener neighborhoods reducing sleep problems, but do not unambiguously support the broader claim that larger spatial scale in design universally and directly reduces PSQI-measured sleep disturbances (and do not address within-home spatial size