regate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'It is possible that larger spatial scales in environmental design directly reduce sleep disturbances, as wide open spaces are thought to promote relaxation and lower stress levels. By living or sleeping in larger areas, people may feel less confined, leading to improved sleep quality and fewer disturbances.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'It is possible that larger spatial scales in environmental design directly reduce sleep disturbances, as wide open spaces are thought to promote relaxation and lower stress levels. By living or sleeping in larger areas, people may feel less confined, leading to improved sleep quality and fewer disturbances.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

