n': 'Rumination, as measured by the CERQ-R, involves reflective thinking that can promote self-awareness and emotional regulation. This enhanced self-regulation is believed to activate anti-inflammatory pathways, such as increased IL-10 production, thereby supporting positive health outcomes. Therefore, higher rumination should be associated with higher levels of anti-inflammatory processes.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Rumination, as measured by the CERQ-R, involves reflective thinking that can promote self-awareness and emotional regulation. This enhanced self-regulation is believed to activate anti-inflammatory pathways, such as increased IL-10 production, thereby supporting positive health outcomes. Therefore, higher rumination should be associated with higher levels of anti-inflammatory processes.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

