ntify and avoid sleep-disrupting factors, such as minor discomfort or subtle noises, thereby directly decreasing sleep disturbance. Conversely, lower mindfulness results in less sensory awareness, causing individuals to overlook potential sleep disruptors and consequently experience more sleep disturbance. This relationship operates independently of other variables in the CLD.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increases in Mindfulness (FFMQ) lead to reduced Sleep disturbance (PSQI) because enhanced mindfulness heightens sensory awareness during nighttime, making individuals more attuned to their bodily sensations and environmental stimuli. This increased perceptual sensitivity allows them to identify and avoid sleep-disrupting factors, such as minor discomfort or subtle noises, thereby directly decreasing sleep disturbance. Conversely, lower mindfulness results in less sensory awareness, causing individuals to overlook potential sleep disruptors and consequently experience more sleep disturbance. This relationship operates independently of other variables in the CLD.', 'perplexity': 1.346192867015557, 'mean_token_prob': 0.829873414871018, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0631094890238339, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0029887137474998997, 'prob_variance': 0.07067152820373268, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9980295761980706, 'avg_nll': 0.2972805099736612}

