75. Perceived social support (MSPSS)-[NEGATIVE]->Rumination (CERQ-R)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Perceived social support (MSPSS) causes rumination (CERQ-R) to change in an inverse relationship. Increasing perceived social support directly reduces the tendency for rumination by providing emotional resources and alternative coping strategies. Conversely, decreased social support can increase rumination as individuals lack external support to buffer negative thoughts. This relationship is direct and not fully mediated by other variables in the system.', 'session_id': '4a4eed24-8545-4e16-9f71-946b0734d107', 'prob_std': 0.2801728457533546, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10915202/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12076526/', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychology/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2024.1330720/full', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3219878/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7488358030961512, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10915202/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited paper shows perceived social support (MSPSS) is associated with lower perceived stress and, via reduced perceived stress, with better mental-health outcomes (anxiety, depression, positive affect). However, it does not measure rumination (CERQ-R) or objective exposure to stressful life events, and its cross‑sectional design precludes causal claims that support “prevents exposure to negative experiences” or that support acts as a shield that directly eliminates triggers for repetitive negative thinking. Thus the general idea that greater perceived support links to reduced stress-related outcomes is supported, but the specific causal mechanism (reduced objective exposure) and the direct effect on rumination are unaddressed."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12076526/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 