ort/multidimensional-scale-of-perceived-social-support-mspss/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited MSPSS source only describes the measurement instrument (items, scales, scoring) for perceived social support. It provides no data, analyses, or discussion linking perceived social support to mindfulness (FFMQ) or describing a causal mechanism by which social support increases trait mindfulness."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://elcentro.sonhs.miami.edu/research/measures-library/mspss/index.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source only describes the MSPSS instrument (items, scoring, translation, psychometric references). It does not present data or discussion linking perceived social support to trait mindfulness (FFMQ) or describe mechanisms (encouragement from others increasing mindfulness), so the claimed relationship is not supported by the provided citation."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0191886919305008", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation contains only an error message and no substantive content about perceived social support or mindfulness, so it does not provide evidence to support or contradict the claimed relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Individuals who perceive higher social support may become more mindful because supportive friends and family encourage them to be present and aware in the moment. This external encouragement directly increases their trait mindfulness, regardless of personal mindfulness practice.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Individuals who perceive higher social support may become more mindful because su